  <div id="byline">27. The Triumph of the Right</div>
  <div id="bodytext">




<figure class="wp-block-image alignwide size-large"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1024" height="512" src="https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/schlafly-1024x512.jpg" alt="A woman speaks before a microphone as demonstrators hold signs reading “Stop ERA” behind her." class="wp-image-1273" srcset="https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/schlafly-1024x512.jpg 1024w, https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/schlafly-300x150.jpg 300w, https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/schlafly-768x384.jpg 768w, https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/schlafly-1536x768.jpg 1536w, https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/schlafly.jpg 1600w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Activist Phyllis Schlafly campaigns against the Equal Rights Amendment in 1978. Bettmann/Corbis.</figcaption></figure>







